# Copy to .env.local for `vercel dev`, or set in the Vercel project's
# Environment Variables settings for the deployed app. Never commit the real
# key — .env.local is already gitignored via *.local.
#
# Get a free-tier key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Supabase (accounts + synced workout history) — both are safe to expose to
# the browser (the anon key only works within the Row Level Security
# policies in supabase/schema.sql, it's not a secret). Leave both blank to
# run with accounts disabled — the app falls back to local-only exactly as
# before. From your Supabase project: Project Settings -> API.
# Must be prefixed VITE_ or Vite won't expose them to the client bundle.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
